What:           /sys/class/power_supply/qcom_qg/device/soc_state
Date:           October 2026
Contact:        Linux power supply mailing list <linux-pm@vger.kernel.org>
Description:
                Read-only diagnostic state of FIFO-based QGauge estimation.
                Boards without FIFO estimation report enabled=0. Otherwise
                a single line contains key=value fields:

                enabled: FIFO estimation is active.
                anchored: an OCV/full anchor has been obtained or restored.
                gap: active uncertainty from missing charge coverage.
                restored: a recent private SDAM record seeded this boot.
                captures/gaps: accepted capture and detected gap counters.
                sampled_ms: accumulated accepted sample duration.
                interval_ms: last ADC sample interval.
                fifo/accum: last completed FIFO and partial sample counts.
                charge_uah: estimated charge in microamp-hours.
                ocv_uv: last accepted hardware OCV, or zero.
                elapsed_ms/duration_ms: last capture wall/sample duration.
                delta_uah: signed charge delta of the last accepted capture.

                Counters start at probe. A historical gap may be recovered
                by an OCV/full anchor, clearing gap without decrementing gaps.
                sampled_ms is not total uptime or proof of sleep coverage.
                These values do not establish measured battery health.
